---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { loadDomains, loadIndex } from "../lib/catalog";
import { FRAMEWORKS, domainLabel } from "../lib/labels";
import scoring from "../../../config/scoring.json";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const index = loadIndex();
const domains = loadDomains();
const order = Object.keys((scoring as { domain_profiles: Record<string, string> }).domain_profiles);
const sorted = [...domains].sort((a, b) => order.indexOf(a.domain) - order.indexOf(b.domain));
const profiles = (scoring as { domain_profiles: Record<string, string> }).domain_profiles;
const frameworks = Object.keys(FRAMEWORKS).length;
const withEvidence = index?.records.filter((r) => r.compliance_summary.some((c) => c.status === "active")).length ?? 0;
const snapshot = index?.snapshot_date ?? "—";
const credit = { 1: "1.0", 2: "0.8", 3: "0.7", 4: "0.3", 5: "0" };
const tiers = [
  ["T1", "Registry-matched", `found in a named authoritative registry, e.g. "Found in FedRAMP Marketplace on ${snapshot}"`, credit[1]],
  ["T2", "Marketplace-listed", "stated in a cloud marketplace compliance field or certification program", credit[2]],
  ["T3", "Document-evidenced", "certificate, letter or AOC reviewed; issuer, number and dates recorded", credit[3]],
  ["T4", "Vendor-claimed", "trust-center statement or machine-readable claim, not yet verified", credit[4]],
  ["T5", "Unknown", "no evidence found. Shown as such, never as non-compliant", credit[5]],
];
---

<Base title="Find agents you can actually trust">
  <script is:inline define:vars={{ base }}>
    // legacy links: /?q=… → /search/?q=…
    if (location.search.includes("q=") || location.search.includes("domain=")) location.replace(`${base}/search/${location.search}`);
  </script>
  <section style="padding: 56px 0 72px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 48px">
    <div>
      <h1>
        <span style="display:block">Find agents you can actually trust.</span>
        <span style="display:block">See the evidence behind every one.</span>
        <span style="display:block; color: var(--accent)">Decide with confidence.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="body" style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 72ch; margin-top: 32px">
        A vendor-neutral registry of AI agents across {domains.length || 12} domains. Agents are identified through Agentic
        Resource Discovery (ARD), Agent2Agent (A2A), Model Context Protocol (MCP) and internal registries. Every result
        leads with a trust profile against the governance frameworks we track for agents: HIPAA, SOC 2, FedRAMP, GDPR,
        ISO/IEC 42001, the EU AI Act and more, each with who issued it, what it covers, whether it is current, and what
        you still have to verify yourself. The catalog is updated weekly.
      </p>
      <div class="row" style="margin-top: 36px; gap: 12px">
        <a class="btn primary" style="min-width: 280px" href={`${base}/domains/`}>Browse a domain Top 100 <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn" href={`${base}/search/`}>Describe what you need</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{domains.length || 12}</div><div class="l">Domains, Top 100 each</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{index?.records.length ?? "—"}</div><div class="l">Resources in the catalog</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{frameworks}</div><div class="l">Compliance frameworks tracked</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{withEvidence}</div><div class="l">Agents with evidence on file</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Pick a domain. Every list is Top 100, ranked by a published formula.</h2>
      <span class="small muted">Snapshot {snapshot} · score version {index?.score_version ?? "sar-score-1.0"}</span>
    </div>
    {sorted.length === 0 ? (
      <p class="notice warn">No catalog is bundled with this build.</p>
    ) : (
      <div class="domain-grid">
        {sorted.map((d, i) => (
          <a href={`${base}/domains/${d.domain}/`}>
            <span class="eyebrow">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")} · {profiles[d.domain] ?? d.profile} profile</span>
            <span class="name">{d.label ?? domainLabel(d.domain)}</span>
            <span class="top">#1 {d.ranked[0]?.name}</span>
            <span class="cta">Top 100 →</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>What it does, in three steps</h2></div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><span class="n">01</span><div><h3>Discover</h3><p>One catalog over GitHub, Hugging Face, the official Model Context Protocol (MCP) Registry, Agentic Resource Discovery (ARD) manifests and cloud marketplaces. Agents are deduplicated, classified into 12 domains and inspected for ARD, Agent2Agent (A2A) and MCP support.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="n">02</span><div><h3>Read the trust profile</h3><p>HIPAA, SOC 2, FedRAMP, GDPR, ISO 42001 and more, each with its source, evidence tier, scope and as-of date. Text only, linked to the origin. Unknown is shown as "No evidence found", never as a failure.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="n">03</span><div><h3>Shortlist and export</h3><p>Filter by must-have compliance, protocol (ARD, A2A, MCP) and license. Compare up to four with the score breakdown. Export CSV or JSON with the sources attached. Shortlists stay in your browser.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="split rev" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 16px">
      <div>
        <h2>One evidence scale, everywhere</h2>
        <p class="body" style="margin-top: 16px; max-width: 44ch">The same five tiers apply to identity, compliance, security and protocol claims. Tier is always written out; color is never the only cue.</p>
        <p class="body" style="margin-top: 12px; max-width: 44ch">Governance credit is earned only after the publisher is verified. A certificate on an unverified publisher shows as "pending publisher verification".</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        {tiers.map(([t, name, desc, c]) => (
          <div class="ledger-row" style="grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr 72px">
            <b>{t}</b>
            <div><b>{name}</b><span class="muted"> — {desc}</span></div>
            <span style="text-align: right; font-weight: 800; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums">{c}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="tiny muted" style="padding-top: 10px">Governance credit per tier. Status overlays (in process, stale, expired, revoked, inherited) earn zero and are shown with their dates.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Why you can rely on it</h2></div>
    <div class="four">
      <div><h4>Open method, MIT code</h4><p>Scoring weights, framework catalog, seed data and every parser are in the public repository. Change goes through reviewed pull requests.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Nothing for sale</h4><p>No payment for inclusion, badges, tier or position. No publisher accounts, no vendor outreach, no hosted service.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Every badge traceable</h4><p>Every badge shows its source link, tier and as-of date, and is re-checked on the schedule its framework file sets. Changes land in the public trust changelog.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Corrections in the open</h4><p>Anyone, including vendors, can file a GitHub issue with a source link. Decisions are recorded in the public trust changelog.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="split rev" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 16px">
      <div>
        <h2>Built for machines too</h2>
        <p class="body" style="margin-top: 16px; max-width: 44ch">The registry conforms to Agentic Resource Discovery (ARD), publishes its own <a href={`${base}/.well-known/ard.json`}>/.well-known/ard.json</a> and, in the self-hosted edition, serves the ARD REST API and wraps search as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool. Search relevance and trust are always separate fields.</p>
      </div>
      <pre class="code"><span class="k">POST</span> /search
&#123; "query": "insurance claims agent, handles PHI",
  "filters": &#123; "framework": "hipaa", "maxTier": 4, "protocol": "mcp" &#125;,
  "limit": 10 &#125;

<span class="c">→ 200</span>  results[].trust   <span class="c">// separate from results[].score and results[].explanation</span></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="band full-bleed">
    <h2><span style="display:block">Copy the code.</span><span style="display:block">Run your own registry.</span><span style="display:block">Scan your own network.</span></h2>
    <div>
      <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.55">The enterprise edition is the same MIT codebase in one self-hosted container: private-network discovery of agents via Agentic Resource Discovery (ARD), Agent2Agent (A2A) and Model Context Protocol (MCP), policy qualification, scheduled scans and an audit trail. Nothing leaves your tenant.</p>
      <div class="row" style="margin-top: 24px; gap: 12px">
        <a class="btn dark" href={`${base}/enterprise/`}>Enterprise edition →</a>
        <a class="btn" href={`${base}/methodology/`}>Read the methodology</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
